{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1557457-shadowland-demesnes-and-the-scope-of-manse-effects","id":1557457,"title":"Shadowland demesnes and the scope of manse effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-10T16:38:03-08:00","id":1557457,"title":"Shadowland demesnes and the scope of manse effects","content":"Hey, y'all!<br /> <br /> I'm running an outcaste DB campaign on a coastal stretch roughly North-Northwest, basically in a <i>much</i> smaller reimagining of the Deshan slave states from 2e. To provide some basic context, the party ran a religious slave revolution and ultimately claimed power, then suffered an apocalyptically pyrrhic victory destroying a Realm naval fleet trying to reclaim the satrapies, which alongside other problems opened up a shadowland in their corner of the Inland Sea.<br /> <br /> Since then they've been biting, clawing and scraping their way out of an unending series of crises while scouting resources and consolidating power, and are finally at a point to start building advantages instead of just being in survival mode. The party necromancer has befriended and recruited the ghosts of some of the dead sailors as privateers, and wants to build on that advantage by using geomancy to turn the shadowland into a demesne and capping it. His vision is for something like an island-fortress of bone that emits a spectral fog to confuse the navigation of ships passing through without the manse owner's permission so they go around in circles until they starve themselves and fall prey to the pirates, both as a further line of defense against Realm reprisal and as something the new state can leverage politically/economically in controlling whose ships can safely pass through.<br /> <br /> My questions are twofold.<br /> <br /> One: does being a shadowland have any impact on which kinds of demesnes can form there? Is it limited to an Abyssal demesne (which, in fairness, may be appropriate for the manse concept anyway) or would a Water demesne be able to form in an aquatic shadowland just fine?<br /> <br /> Two: is his idea within the scope of things a 3-dot manse could do, by 3e standards? And if not, do you have any ideas for drawbacks or alternatives that could give him something like what he wants while fitting better within those limitations? I can't find a lot of guidance on how powerful or far-reaching manse effects can be in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","name":"MJ6373","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T12:22:50-08:00","id":1557475,"title":"","content":"I'm away from my books at the moment, so I can only give provisional answers. I'd have a mind to check my point later. With that in mind:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MJ6373</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1557457-shadowland-demesnes-and-the-scope-of-manse-effects#post1557457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One: does being a shadowland have any impact on which kinds of demesnes can form there? Is it limited to an Abyssal demesne (which, in fairness, may be appropriate for the manse concept anyway) or would a Water demesne be able to form in an aquatic shadowland just fine?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm sure it would have an impact, I don't recall Sworn to the Grave saying that only Abyssal demesnes can form in shadowlands. Even if it did, it's not particularly out of order to have one show up for the use of narrative under a premise of being something out of the ordinary or artificially maintained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MJ6373</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two: is his idea within the scope of things a 3-dot manse could do, by 3e standards? And if not, do you have any ideas for drawbacks or alternatives that could give him something like what he wants while fitting better within those limitations? I can't find a lot of guidance on how powerful or far-reaching manse effects can be in this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remind me, do manses only come in two scales and three-dots is the lesser one?<br /> <br /> In the absence of rules for what the powers of manses can be, I'd look to the scope of hearthstones as a provisional guideline. I know there's one that can have an effect to improve fertility in a radius of miles. If that's lesser, I'd say it's valid to have a manse of similar power possess capabilities of similar providence and greater scope, on the premise of being fuelled by the direct geomancy and offset by being completely stationary.<br /> <br /> If the hearthstone is not... then same premise, just with maybe a reduced scope. Maybe broader, but the manse has special requirements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T21:01:53-08:00","id":1557495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1557457-shadowland-demesnes-and-the-scope-of-manse-effects?p=1557475#post1557475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind me, do manses only come in two scales and three-dots is the lesser one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, 3-dot, 5-dot and Legendary, but yes, 3-dots are the smallest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1557457-shadowland-demesnes-and-the-scope-of-manse-effects?p=1557475#post1557475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the absence of rules for what the powers of manses can be, I'd look to the scope of hearthstones as a provisional guideline. I know there's one that can have an effect to improve fertility in a radius of miles. If that's lesser, I'd say it's valid to have a manse of similar power possess capabilities of similar providence and greater scope, on the premise of being fuelled by the direct geomancy and offset by being completely stationary.<br /> <br /> If the hearthstone is not... then same premise, just with maybe a reduced scope. Maybe broader, but the manse has special requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every type of standard hearthstone (the kind 3-dot manses make) has an example effect in core that affects 2-4 miles around, though these are mostly utility effects that reduce the threat of ordinary hazards - structural collapse, fire, poisoned/diseased water, bad luck, that sort of thing. The Abyssal one lets people in three miles talk to dead relatives at their graves, so mild supernatural effects aside from mundane threat protection are clearly on the table.<br /> <br /> That's arguably less overt than the fog thing, but regular old spooky fog could easily be an ordinary demesne emanation, and rephrased as a sort of inversion where the risks of boating accidents and navigation failures are subtly increased rather than ameliorated, it doesn't sound out of scope. Thanks for the advice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","name":"MJ6373","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T12:16:39-08:00","id":1557523,"title":"","content":"Yeah, on review, I'm thinking that a standard manse shouldn't be capable of projecting an effect that is highly imposing upon those within its proximity, and the idea of pivoting towards &quot;relatively mundane, if spooky&quot; fog that the characters then need to leverage is the right call.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it would not be out of order to enhance the power of a structure a bit beyond its weight class by means of adding greater impositions to sustain it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T08:49:23-08:00","id":1557678,"title":"","content":"Offhand, five elements, as well as elementally aspected leylines and demesnes also exist in the Underworld, but those are dark/deathly mirrors of the Creation's elements.So, while elemental demesnes amd manses (not just abyssal ones) are definitely possible, one need to remember that they would be <i>different</i>. <br /> Shadowlands, being placed between those two realms, can posess both Underworld elements as well as Creation ones.So, yes, there can be a Water demesne, and shape and effects would depend on which realm you'd use as basis for it.<br /> Notice, though, that this choice has meaning. Geomancy is one of the ways citizens of creation have to confront and contain shadowlands. Promoting the flow of energies of creation would be hard, but once done would help in diminishing effects of the Underworld on the terrain. The opposite is however also true - promote the flow of Underworld energies, and you will be helping Shadowland to spread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T15:36:46-08:00","id":1557690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1557457-shadowland-demesnes-and-the-scope-of-manse-effects?p=1557523#post1557523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, on review, I'm thinking that a standard manse shouldn't be capable of projecting an effect that is highly imposing upon those within its proximity, and the idea of pivoting towards &quot;relatively mundane, if spooky&quot; fog that the characters then need to leverage is the right call.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it would not be out of order to enhance the power of a structure a bit beyond its weight class by means of adding greater impositions to sustain it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sustainance conditions in exchange for a somewhat heavier effect sounds good, I'll pitch it to him. I was also thinking of suggesting different conditions to give it other ways to be bypassed. Like, instead of requiring active manse owner approval to avoid whatever misdirection or naval bad luck we go with, it's just undead guidance, and the necromancer's leverage comes from basically arranging whether the ghost pirates will target a given ship or escort it, making the route <i>safer</i> from some ordinary hazards as the metaphorical carrot.<br /> <br /> Which centers the ghosts more, and leaves some extra vulnerabilities e.g. people figuring out the weakness and bringing their own undead help, or characters with certain leverage and social prowess convincing or bribing the ghosts there into being helpful to them without the necromancer's approval.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1557457-shadowland-demesnes-and-the-scope-of-manse-effects?p=1557678#post1557678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notice, though, that this choice has meaning. Geomancy is one of the ways citizens of creation have to confront and contain shadowlands. Promoting the flow of energies of creation would be hard, but once done would help in diminishing effects of the Underworld on the terrain. The opposite is however also true - promote the flow of Underworld energies, and you will be helping Shadowland to spread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's an interesting point, I sorta forgot about that.<br /> <br /> I think that makes the decision all the more interesting, so I'll bring it up to the player. Making the shadowland bigger would make the scheme work better by giving the ghost-pirates a larger ranging area, in exchange for all the general worldly consequences of bigger shadowlands (and making the place an appealing target for a deathknight or nephwrack or something). The alternative is more pro-social, but puts the big advantage being worked for here on a timer. Thanks for reminding me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","name":"MJ6373","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}